      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report the case of a 58-year-old man with coronary vasospasm that occurred within an anomalous coronary artery. The rapidly progressive clinical course and the dramatic treadmill test result preceeded the diagnostic cardiac catheterization. Combination therapy with isosorbide, beta blocker, and nifedipine resulted in complete resolution of symptoms."},
